damentals only.", "No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "New Hampshire's 2028 presidential contest is an open race after two terms of a Republican president, and the state's partisan lean favors Democrats by about two points. No general-election polls, expert ratings, fundraising figures, or market prices are yet available, so the picture rests on fundamentals alone.\n\nThe forecast gives Democrats a narrow edge consistent with the state's lean, but uncertainty is wide because neither party's nominee is known and the primary fields on both sides remain fluid. Headlines show 2028 contenders like Pritzker, Harris, and Newsom already campaigning, but none of that yet translates into a measurable general-election advantage. Small shifts in the national environment or nominee selection could move this race readily.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.5965, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.5716, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.5791, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.5682, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.5806, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.5778, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.5749, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.5779, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.5754, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.5715, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.5679, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.5729, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.5769, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.572, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.5668, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.5746, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.5705, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.5764, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.5707, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-12", "p_dem": 0.569